      "applicability": "established",
      "finding": "conditional_qualified",
      "comment": "Clause 3.3 allows a conditional licence if there is no recent history of a 'severe hypoglycaemic event' and the person experiences early warning symptoms. Paragraph 1 describes an episode where he became sweaty and confused after skipping lunch, requiring assistance to obtain a sweet drink; this indicates awareness of hypoglycaemia (early warning symptom) rather than a loss of consciousness."
    },
    {
      "source_slot": 5,
      "patient_paragraph": 1,
      "applicability": "established",
      "finding": "conditional_qualified",
      "comment": "Clause 3.3 requires a treatment regimen that minimises the risk of hypoglycaemia. Paragraph 1 states he injects insulin each evening; while the specific preparation is unknown, the existence of an insulin regimen constitutes a documented treatment plan."
    },
    {
      "source_slot": 5,
      "patient_paragraph": 2,
      "applicability": "established",
      "finding": "conditional_qualified",
      "comment": "Clause 3.3 requires an absence of end-organ effects affecting driving (vision, heart, nerves). Paragraph 2 notes a glucose value of 3.1 mmol/L recorded after drinking and denies passing out; there is no evidence provided in the note of end-organ damage."
    },
    {
      "source_slot": 5,
      "patient_paragraph": 2,
      "applicability": "established",
      "finding": "conditional_qualified",
      "comment": "Clause 3.3 requires an annual review by a specialist (endocrinologist or consultant physician). Paragraph 1 states he cannot name the insulin preparation or dose, and Paragraph 2 states he is waiting for endocrinology review; this indicates the prerequisite specialist assessment has not yet been completed."
    },
    {
      "source_slot": 5,
